{
  "$comment": "Mask Composite's and Video Overlay's quote before a run when what reaches them is made by another node — read by BOTH estimates over the same graphs, through the one measured walk (`measuredWireLengthSec`, @nodaro/render-rules): the editor's (frontend maskCompositePricingUnits / videoOverlayPricingUnits — the node's pill, its Run button, the confirm and the workflow badge) and the server's workflow estimate (CreditsService.estimateWorkflowCreditsAt, the composite's own line). Each case wires its sources into the step `c` (an edge with no `target` goes into `c`), which is a Mask Composite with default settings, or a Video Overlay with one stored video layer (so it quotes on its video row) and the case's `video` wire as its base. `expectedUnits` holds the 5-second units both quote, for two run sets (and, where a case gives `partial`, a third: exactly its `runSet`, passed as the editor's run set and the server's `runNodeIds`): `whole` (the editor's whole-run badge and confirm, which pass every executable node, frozen ones included; the server's estimate with no run set, which leaves frozen nodes out) and `alone` (the step's own Run and its pill on the editor; a server run of only `c`). Mask Composite's cap is 60 units (300 s), Video Overlay's 12 (60 s). A video made in the run is read at its planned length plus each step's slack once for every clip a node makes on the way (0.1 s on Mask Composite, which charges the container; 1/24 s on Video Overlay, which charges the video stream) — a step that only passes its input on adds none; a node that does not run hands on its take, at the length recorded with it.",
  "cases": [
    {
